**One deliberate choice:** I have **not** ignored `static/`. Your JavaScript belongs there and should be committed to GitHub. I have also ignored trained model artifacts and datasets because they should generally be obtained/generated separately rather than committed into the repository.

---

## GitHub repository

### Repository name

**`nutrivision`**

### Repository title

**NutriVision — Food Recognition & Nutrition Intelligence Platform**

### Repository description

**Django-based food recognition and nutrition platform powered by EfficientNetB0, PostgreSQL, JWT authentication, Celery, Redis, and REST APIs.**

### Suggested GitHub topics

```text
python
django
django-rest-framework
tensorflow
keras
efficientnet
computer-vision
deep-learning
food-recognition
image-classification
postgresql
redis
celery
jwt
jquery
bootstrap
machine-learning
transfer-learning
````

### Suggested repository structure

```text
nutrivision
│
├── Django Backend
├── EfficientNetB0 ML Pipeline
├── PostgreSQL Persistence
├── JWT + Session Authentication
├── REST API
├── Redis + Celery
├── Nutrition Lookup
└── Bootstrap + jQuery Frontend
```

One point I would preserve in the implementation: **Food-101 should be the image-classification dataset, while nutrition data should be a separate data source/model layer.** That separation will prevent the project from making the technically incorrect claim that EfficientNetB0 itself predicts calories from an image.
